SERVICE AGREEMENT

This Service Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into as of [Date] by and between [Company A] ("Provider") and [Company B] ("Client").

ARTICLE 1 - SCOPE OF SERVICES
The Provider agrees to deliver software development services as described in Exhibit A.

ARTICLE 2 - PAYMENT TERMS
2.1 The Client shall pay all invoices within 30 days of receipt.
2.2 Late payments will incur a penalty of 5% per month on the outstanding balance.
2.3 All fees are non-refundable under any circumstances.
2.4 The Provider reserves the right to suspend services if payment is not received within 15 days.

ARTICLE 3 - LIABILITY
3.1 The Provider's total liability under this Agreement shall not exceed the total fees paid by the Client.
3.2 IN NO EVENT SHALL THE PROVIDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR BUSINESS OPPORTUNITIES.
3.3 The Client agrees to indemnify and hold harmless the Provider from any and all claims, damages, losses, and expenses arising from the Client's use of the services.

ARTICLE 4 - TERMINATION
4.1 Either party may terminate this Agreement with 90 days written notice.
4.2 The Provider may terminate this Agreement immediately and without notice for any breach by the Client.
4.3 Upon termination, the Client shall pay all outstanding fees within 7 days.
4.4 All rights granted to the Client under this Agreement shall immediately revert to the Provider.

ARTICLE 5 - AUTO-RENEWAL
5.1 This Agreement shall automatically renew for successive one-year periods unless either party provides written notice of non-renewal at least 60 days before the end of the current term.
5.2 Renewal terms may be modified by the Provider at any time with 30 days notice.

ARTICLE 6 - INDEMNIFICATION
6.1 The Client shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Provider, its officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or relating to the Client's breach of this Agreement or use of the services.
6.2 The Provider shall have no obligation to indemnify the Client for any reason whatsoever.

ARTICLE 7 - GOVERNING LAW
7.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware.
7.2 Any dispute arising under this Agreement shall be resolved exclusively in the courts of Delaware.
7.3 The Client waive any right to participate in class action lawsuits against the Provider.

ARTICLE 8 - CONFIDENTIALITY
8.1 The Client shall maintain the confidentiality of all proprietary information disclosed by the Provider.
8.2 This confidentiality obligation shall survive termination of this Agreement for a period of 5 years.

ARTICLE 9 - INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
9.1 All intellectual property created by the Provider in connection with the services shall be the exclusive property of the Provider.
9.2 The Client shall have no right, title, or interest in any deliverables or work product.

ARTICLE 10 - FORCE MAJEURE
10.1 Neither party shall be liable for any delay or failure to perform resulting from causes beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, war, terrorism, or pandemic.

ARTICLE 11 - ENTIRE AGREEMENT
This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the parties and supersedes all prior negotiations, representations, or agreements.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first above written.
